.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt PLAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm play
.Nd play a PCM16 WAV file through the audio: scheme
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar file.wav
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one RIFF PCM16 WAV file (mono or stereo, 8 kHz to 192 kHz), selects the stream format on
.Dv audio:out0
and writes the samples through the scheme.
The null sink consumes the stream; a driver-backed sink is the HDA path (B44).
.Pp
The final line reports the frame count, sample rate and channel count.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The file was written and drained.
.It 1
The file could not be parsed, or the audio server returned an error.
.It 2
Usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ play /etc/tone440.wav
.Dl play: ok 24000 frames, 48000 Hz, 2 channels
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr beep 1 ,
.Xr mixer 1 ,
.Xr audiod 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
